# How Spring Boot finds a post-processor that has to run before any bean exists: `spring.factories`, under the
# interface's own name. Spring Boot 4 reads `org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor` here (and the
# deprecated `boot.env` key), and no `.imports` file for post-processors at all. Comma-separated, one entry.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=com.example.deliverystarter.config.DatabaseUrlEnvironmentPostProcessor
